      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Recombinant tPA (alteplase) can be used up to 3 hrs after onset if there are ⍉contraindications; some experts recommend up to 4.5 hrs, w additional exclusion criteria b/n 3 and 4.5 hrs; tPA must be given "
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       },
       {
        "type": "highlight",
        "attrs": {
         "hex": "FF0000"
        }
       }
      ],
      "text": "w.in 4.5 hrs"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": ", timed from when the pt was last observed to be well"
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "tPA dose 0.9 mg/kg IV (max 90 mg): 10% by rapid IV inj over 1 min, the rest over 60 minutes; anticoagulants and antiplatelets are ⍉used w.in 24 hrs of tPA"
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
